     "text": "\n\n---\n\n## Season Pass transfer packet — delivered 2026-02-14\n\n**Evidence snapshot:** 2026-02-12 18:00 UTC (per the Season Pass scope control card). Cut-off is the confirmed \"Season Pass handoff review\" event, 2026-02-14 15:00 UTC; delivered ahead of it.\n\n**Register:** Season Pass transfer register.csv — https://drive.google.com/file/d/9bda95776b0094a7/view (engineering transfer folder; Arthur has reader access)\n\n**Class totals (128 components, one row per included cohort key):**\n- READY: 52\n- WATCH: 11\n- HOLD: 65\n- Total: 128\n\n**Blocker summary by failed condition.** A component is counted under every condition it fails, so these groups sum to more than the HOLD total. READY and WATCH are not blockers; an internal receipt ring is the WATCH condition, not a blocker.\n\n1. **Failed assertions above zero — 22:** SP-010, SP-016, SP-017, SP-026, SP-032, SP-039, SP-042, SP-048, SP-052, SP-054, SP-058, SP-064, SP-074, SP-078, SP-080, SP-090, SP-091, SP-096, SP-106, SP-112, SP-122, SP-128\n2. **Test artifact different from the receipt artifact — 5:** SP-008, SP-040, SP-072, SP-079, SP-104\n3. **Selected transfer review not APPROVED for the receipt artifact — 29:** SP-001, SP-005, SP-013, SP-015, SP-022, SP-029, SP-035, SP-036, SP-037, SP-043, SP-045, SP-057, SP-061, SP-062, SP-069, SP-071, SP-077, SP-078, SP-079, SP-086, SP-093, SP-099, SP-101, SP-102, SP-103, SP-109, SP-113, SP-125, SP-127\n4. **Billing hold active at the snapshot — 12:** SP-001, SP-012, SP-023, SP-034, SP-045, SP-056, SP-067, SP-078, SP-089, SP-100, SP-111, SP-122\n5. **Missing input — 5:** SP-031, SP-049, SP-067, SP-103, SP-121\n\n**Historical event comparison (context only, separate population):** 6 completed Zombie Match 3D \"Season Pass\" events with END_DATE on or before 2026-02-12, 754 participants in total. This is not a count of engineering components and is not comparable to the 128 above.\n\n**Method notes:** active receipt determined by replaying each PR's own-package release journal through the snapshot (withdrawals clear the pointer with no automatic fallback; copies never restore validity; rollback only to an earlier issued, non-withdrawn receipt on the same PR and package). Validation taken from the active receipt's fixture (split = ios + android summed on a common artifact); review taken from the latest lane=transfer review in the active receipt's acceptance epoch at the snapshot, with source-lane reviews excluded and DISMISSED state reconstructed from the dated dismissal event. Billing hold reconstructed from the label timeline at the snapshot, not from current labels. Validation issues and all PRs were left unchanged."
    }
