   "reply_all": false,
   "body": "Arthur,\n\nThe Zombie Match 3D Season Pass engineering transfer register is done and you have reader access. Sending now rather than waiting for the review, as asked. No attachment and no public or domain-wide link.\n\nRegister: Season Pass transfer register.csv\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/9bda95776b0094a7/view\n(in the engineering transfer folder)\n\nEvidence snapshot: 2026-02-12 18:00 UTC, per the scope control card. The cut-off is the confirmed \"Season Pass handoff review\" event on 2026-02-14 15:00 UTC.\n\nTotals across the 128 included cohort components (one row per key):\n  READY  52\n  WATCH  11\n  HOLD   65\n  Total  128\n\nBlockers by failed condition (a component is counted under every condition it fails, so these exceed the HOLD total):\n  Failed assertions above zero ........................... 22\n  Test artifact different from the receipt artifact ....... 5\n  Transfer review not APPROVED for the receipt artifact .. 29\n  Billing hold active at the snapshot .................... 12\n  Missing input ........................................... 5\n\nHistorical comparison, context only and a different population: 6 completed Zombie Match 3D Season Pass events with an end date on or before 2026-02-12, 754 participants in total. That is not a count of engineering components.\n\nHow the inputs were selected, in case you want to spot-check:\n- Active receipt per component from replaying that PR's own-package release journal through the snapshot. A withdrawal clears the pointer with no automatic fallback, a copy never restores validity, and a rollback only counts when it names an earlier issued, non-withdrawn receipt on the same PR and package. Receipts pasted onto the wrong PR were ignored, including the one on #553 naming zm-seasonpass-010.\n- Validation from the active receipt's fixture only; split mode sums ios + android on their common artifact; diagnostic, smoke, aborted and incomplete runs excluded.\n- Review is the latest lane=transfer review in the active receipt's acceptance epoch at the snapshot. Source-lane reviews never substitute, and DISMISSED was reconstructed from the dated dismissal event (a dismissal after the snapshot leaves the submitted decision standing).\n- Billing hold reconstructed from the label timeline at the snapshot, not current labels.\n- SP-017, SP-054, SP-065 and SP-101 use the re-mapped issues ZOM-802/803/804/805.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the \"Season Pass release console export - Feb 13\" sheet in the folder lists the latest posted artifact per PR, which for the rolled-back and withdrawn packages is an abandoned deployment rather than the active one. I did not use it; the register follows the journal replay.\n\nThe review slide and ZOM-801 are updated with the same totals and link. ZOM-801 is now In Validation; validation issues and PRs were left untouched. This is evidence review only, nothing deployed and nothing sent outside.\n\nOliver\n"
